{"_id":"6904c8b3166b018f83dfed44","roadmapSlug":"shell-bash","nodeId":"sYzelzBxQUcz5bK1HVWam","description":"# Comments\n\nComments are explanatory notes added to code to make it easier to understand. They are ignored by the interpreter or compiler, meaning they don't affect how the program runs. They are primarily for human readers to understand the purpose and logic behind the code.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Writing Comments in Bash Scripts","url":"https://linuxize.com/post/bash-comments/","_id":"6a7f4b52cb44947debcff051"},{"type":"article","title":"How to Comment in Bash","url":"https://phoenixnap.com/kb/bash-comment","_id":"6a7f4b52cb44947debcff052"},{"type":"video","title":"Comments - Bash Scripting","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ky9AiwIeORA","_id":"6a7f4b52cb44947debcff053"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-31T14:33:23.601Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:30.660Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/shell-bash/content/sYzelzBxQUcz5bK1HVWam.md"}